# Copy to .env (or .env.local) and fill in. Vite only exposes vars prefixed with VITE_.
# These are BUILD-TIME values — set them before `npm run build`. They are baked into
# the client bundle, so do NOT put secrets here. (OAuth client IDs are public by design.)

# API Proxy Worker (optional, Phase 1.5 Track A). When set, ALL external finance APIs (Yahoo, MFAPI,
# NPS, IPO, vehicle) route through the Penny API Proxy Worker — fixes CORS, adds shared caching, and
# enables the vehicle queue. Unset = direct calls (today's no-backend behavior). Setup:
# workers/api-proxy/README.md
# VITE_API_PROXY=https://penny-api-proxy.your-subdomain.workers.dev

# Yahoo Finance proxy (optional, legacy). Used only when VITE_API_PROXY is NOT set. In dev, requests
# otherwise fall back to the Vite proxy at /api/yf.
# VITE_YF_PROXY=https://your-worker.example.workers.dev

# Google Drive backup (optional). When set, the "Back up to Google Drive" option in
# Backup & Restore activates. This is the developer/deployment config — one OAuth client
# ID per origin; each user signs into their own Google account. See docs/features/backup.md.
# Enabling Drive ALSO requires adding these to the CSP in index.html:
#   script-src  … https://accounts.google.com
#   connect-src … https://www.googleapis.com https://accounts.google.com
# VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com
